    "answer": {
      "short": "Yes. Both produce a $180^\\circ$ rotation of $y=f(x)$ about the origin.",
      "worked": "Bob reflects in the $x$-axis, then the $y$-axis:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=-f(x)\\\\y&=-f(-x)\\end{align*}$$\nMary reflects in the $y$-axis, then the $x$-axis:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=f(-x)\\\\y&=-f(-x)\\end{align*}$$\nYes. Both produce $y=-f(-x)$, a $180^\\circ$ rotation about the origin.",
